haha, and it's also a good lesson:

Listen up nintadni because I STILL make this mistake regularly.  se te ve xe
are the "swapping" cmavo.  The rafsi of these cmavo are sel te*r* vel xel
respectively.  meanwhile te*l* is the rafsi for stela.  Do not think that if
you say {teldunda} you are saying {te dunda}, you are in fact saying {stela
zei dunda}.

ta'onai yeah, right on selkik.  I recently made use of cei in a way that I
really kind of NEEDED it.  Upon thinking about it I wondered "if to express
this in lojban I required cei to assign like 3 different bridi to shortcut
variables... how the hell would I have said this in english?!"  And sure
enough, it was not an easy thing at all to say in english.

